<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Las Carreras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1849">1849</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-war-of-independence">Dominican War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Las Carreras was fought in April 1849 near Baní in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a>, where Dominican forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-santana">Pedro Santana</a> defeated the invading Haitian army of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque">Faustin Soulouque</a>. The victory checked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>'s attempts to reconquer the eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a>. Soulouque, who later ruled as Emperor Faustin I, invaded again in 1855–1856 and was again defeated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-las-carreras.jpg" alt="Battle of Las Carreras" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mariano Torrente · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_de_las_Carreras_ganada_por_el_general_de_divisi%C3%B3n_Pedro_Santana_el_d%C3%ADa_21_de_abril_de_1849,_contra_los_haitianos_mandados_por_el_general_Soulouque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
